   "html_text": "In the chapter where Johannsen introduced the terms “genotype”, “phenotype”, and “gene”, he begins by first exploring the meaning of the term “type” as suggested by Adolphe Quetelet. When measuring some character which varies across individuals in a population, the type according to Johannsen refers to “the mean value or the center of variation” for the measured character (1909: 116). For variable traits that are binomially distributed, there is only one central tendency, so Johannsen calls thes",
